From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:27:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: do not write the encoder frame size on MFC
 v15
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MFC v15 has no E_FRAME_WIDTH and E_FRAME_HEIGHT: 0xF770 and 0xF774 are
the decoder's payload registers there. The encoder takes the cropped size
only, as in Google's exynos-mfc driver (kernel/google-modules/soc/gs,
drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc/, branch
android-gs-pantah-6.1-android16). The other encoder registers that
s5p-mfc writes match that driver's mfc_regs.h by address, 76 of 76.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c | 20 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
index 6d764254b..683027fea 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
@@ -913,10 +913,17 @@ static int s5p_mfc_set_enc_params(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx)
 
 	mfc_debug_enter();
 
-	/* width */
-	writel(ctx->img_width, mfc_regs->e_frame_width); /* 16 align */
-	/* height */
-	writel(ctx->img_height, mfc_regs->e_frame_height); /* 16 align */
+	/*
+	 * MFC v15 has no frame width and height registers: the encoder
+	 * takes the cropped size, and 0xF770/0xF774 are the decoder's
+	 * payload registers there (as in Google's exynos-mfc driver).
+	 */
+	if (!IS_MFCV15(dev)) {
+		/* width */
+		writel(ctx->img_width, mfc_regs->e_frame_width); /* 16 align */
+		/* height */
+		writel(ctx->img_height, mfc_regs->e_frame_height); /* 16 align */
+	}
 
 	/* cropped width */
 	writel(ctx->img_width, mfc_regs->e_cropped_frame_width);
@@ -1191,8 +1198,9 @@ static int s5p_mfc_set_enc_params_h264(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx)
 
 	/* height */
 	if (p_h264->interlace) {
-		writel(ctx->img_height >> 1,
-				mfc_regs->e_frame_height); /* 32 align */
+		if (!IS_MFCV15(dev))
+			writel(ctx->img_height >> 1,
+			       mfc_regs->e_frame_height); /* 32 align */
 		/* cropped height */
 		writel(ctx->img_height >> 1,
 				mfc_regs->e_cropped_frame_height);
